## Cookie Policy
Ai Digital Services (operating as Automation.Ai)
Last Updated: March 3, 2026
At Ai Digital Services, we value your privacy and aim to be completely transparent about how we utilize tracking technology. This policy outlines how cookies are used to enhance your experience on our automated platform.
## 1. What Are Cookies?
Cookies are small configuration files saved onto your computer or mobile device when you browse online. They help sites remember options, ensure security, and provide clean interaction dynamics.
## 2. How We Categorize Cookies
We group cookies depending on their specific technical purpose:

* Strictly Necessary: Essential tools deployed automatically to maintain basic site actions, security protections (such as CSRF validation tokens), and user login flows.
* Performance & Analytics: Tools used exclusively to compile anonymous traffic charts, error reporting, and visitor paths (utilizing privacy-centric tools such as Plausible or Google Analytics).
* Advertising & Marketing Signals: When active, these mechanisms communicate signals directly to platform networks (like Google Tags) to manage campaign performance tracking or ad personalization. We do not deploy these unless you actively provide explicit consent.

## 3. Google Consent Mode v2 Alignment
In compliance with international regulations and Google's updated data frameworks, our website utilizes an integrated interactive consent barrier. When you update your choices, the system modifies these four operational permissions in real-time:

* analytics_storage (Controls tracking analytics)
* ad_storage (Controls cookie advertising storage)
* ad_user_data (Manages user profile traits relayed to Google networks)
* ad_personalization (Governs tailored target-remarketing algorithms)

## 4. Direct Choice Management
You maintain absolute authority over your choices at any point:

* On Our Site: You can reset your permissions universally by clicking the "Manage Cookie Preferences" link embedded natively in our website footer layout.
* Browser Control: You can set your browser preferences to universally filter, flag, or completely reject cookies. Be aware that removing baseline functional elements may disrupt structural features across your session.

## 5. Third-Party Integrations
Some third-party tools embedded within our channels (such as social profile logins or external communication frameworks) maintain unique processing standards. We advise checking their independent compliance documentation directly.
